    "text": "Most modern machine learning paradigms abstract away temporal pressures, treating memory as static storage and separating learning from the irreversible trajectory of the learner.",
    "topic": "Memory abstraction in machine learning"
  },
  {
    "text": "Persistent interaction, adaptation, memory, and decision-making over time are increasingly required for deployed machine learning systems.",
    "topic": "Temporal requirements of machine learning systems"
  },
  {
    "text": "WorldDirector introduces persistent dynamic object memory to enable controllable world simulators without continuous visual observation.",
    "topic": "WorldDirector's persistent dynamic object memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "ReContext addresses long-context reasoning failures in large language models by recursively replaying evidence to utilize relevant information already present in their inputs.",
    "topic": "ReContext's recursive evidence replay for long-context reasoning"
  },
  {
    "text": "Cross-agent memory governance can be managed using the Reflective Context Governor transplanted onto agent memory (memgov v0.1.0).",
    "topic": "Cross-agent memory governance with memgov"
  }
